# nguo-3d — line endings, binary marking, and Git LFS.
# SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-or-later

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 1. Text normalisation
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Everything git detects as text is stored LF and checked out LF, on every
# platform. Without this a Windows contributor's editor turns a .wgsl shader or
# a golden .json fixture into CRLF, and the byte-exact regression tests fail for
# reasons that have nothing to do with the change. Verified 2026-08-02: no file
# in the tree currently contains a CR, so this is a no-op today and a guard
# from here on.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Explicit, so detection never has to guess on our own source.
*.rs      text eol=lf
*.wgsl    text eol=lf
*.toml    text eol=lf
*.md      text eol=lf
*.json    text eol=lf
*.py      text eol=lf
*.sh      text eol=lf
*.cpp     text eol=lf
*.hpp     text eol=lf
*.h       text eol=lf
*.svg     text eol=lf
*.yml     text eol=lf
# Wavefront .obj, COLLADA .dae and USD .usda are ASCII formats — text, not binary.
*.obj     text eol=lf
*.dae     text eol=lf
*.usda    text eol=lf

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 2. Binary — never diffed, never EOL-mangled
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.png     binary
*.jpg     binary
*.jpeg    binary
*.ico     binary
*.icns    binary
*.ttf     binary
*.otf     binary
*.woff    binary
*.woff2   binary
*.glb     binary
*.vrm     binary
*.npy     binary
*.pdf     binary

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 3. Git LFS — prospective
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# None of these extensions exist in the committable tree today (2026-08-02:
# 712 files, 11.7 MB, largest is 1.6 MB). Every real asset of these kinds
# currently lives under samples/ or instructions/, which the root .gitignore
# excludes. These rules exist so that the first time a garment source, an HDRI
# or a UI-reference capture *is* committed, it lands in LFS instead of being
# baked into history where it cannot be removed.
#
# Deliberately NOT listed as bare extensions: *.png, *.ttf, *.svg, *.glb,
# *.obj. See §3b (path-scoped instead) and §4 (never).
*.blend   filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.blend1  filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.fbx     filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.zprj    filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.exr     filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.hdr     filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.rar     filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.zip     filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.7z      filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.mp4     filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.mov     filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.wav     filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 3b. Git LFS — the avatar bundle (re-measured 2026-08-03, SECOND bundle)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The bundle was REPLACED. The first one was 223 MB / 94 files, flat, four
# avatars, bodies of unverified provenance. This one is 227 MB / 68 files, two
# avatars, nested, and Seede XR owns the bodies outright (LICENSING.md §4).
# The block below was re-derived against the new tree, not carried over.
#
# Measured with `du -k` on 2026-08-03 — 68 files, 232 760 KB (227.3 MiB),
# against 716 tracked files for the entire rest of the repo:
#
#   avatars/glb/            127 568 KB   124.6 MiB    6 x .glb
#   avatars/vrm/             50 268 KB    49.1 MiB    2 x .vrm
#   textures/skin/shared/    30 368 KB    29.7 MiB    7 x .png  (normal/AO/rough/...)
#   textures/skin/tones/     19 060 KB    18.6 MiB   10 x .png  (MST01..MST10 albedo)
#   previews/                 5 276 KB     5.2 MiB   11 x .png
#   data/                       172 KB               28 x .json
#   README.md + docs/            48 KB                4 x .md
#
# So 232 540 KB (99.91 %) is .glb/.vrm/.png and 220 KB (0.09 %) is text. LFS
# takes the first group and nothing else. The 28 JSON (manifest, rig, bone map,
# UVs, LOD/animation/export metadata, MST tone values) and the 4 Markdown stay
# in NORMAL GIT — 220 KB total, they diff, and they are by far the most
# reviewable part of the bundle. Routing them to LFS would make the licensing
# and rig metadata unreadable in a PR to buy back 0.09 % of the bytes.
#
# Two repo-side files were added next to the bundle and are also normal git:
# `assets/avatars/LICENSE.md` (the licence record) and
# `assets/avatars/LICENSES/CC-BY-4.0.txt` (18 657 bytes, the canonical CC BY 4.0
# legal text — the assets are CC BY 4.0, see LICENSING.md §0). A licence text
# that only exists as an LFS pointer would not satisfy anything, so no rule here
# may ever route *.txt or *.md under assets/avatars/ to LFS.
#
# The three globs below are unchanged from the first bundle, and that is a
# verified result rather than an assumption: `git check-attr filter` over all
# 68 files gives filter=lfs for exactly 36 (6 glb + 2 vrm + 28 png) and
# unspecified for exactly 32 (28 json + 4 md). `**` matches zero or more
# directories, so the new nested `avatars/glb/`, `avatars/vrm/` and
# `textures/skin/{shared,tones}/` are covered without a per-directory rule.
#
# Rules are PATH-SCOPED, not bare-extension, on purpose: a bare `*.png` would
# also swallow ui/assets/images/splash_screen_image.png and the icon SVGs'
# neighbours, which §4 forbids. Scoping means §4 does not have to fight §3b.
#
# Safe to LFS because these are RUNTIME-loaded, never embedded at compile time.
# Re-verified 2026-08-03 — `grep -rn 'include_bytes!\|include_str!'
# --include=*.rs` over core-engine/ ui/ bridges/ tools/ gives 5 real
# `include_bytes!` sites, ALL under ui/assets/ (splash PNG, brand SVG, Inter
# TTF, Space Mono TTF, the icons macro), and every `include_str!` is a *.wgsl
# shader. ZERO hits reference assets/avatars/. The bundle is opened at run time
# by nguo_avatar (ui/crates/nguo-avatar/src/lib.rs:266-272, path from
# $NGUO_AVATAR_BUNDLE or <repo>/assets/avatars), which returns an error for a
# bad file — an LFS pointer fails loudly there instead of silently becoming the
# mesh. See §4 for why that distinction is load-bearing.
assets/avatars/**/*.glb filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
assets/avatars/**/*.vrm filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
assets/avatars/**/*.png filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 4. Build-time embedded assets — MUST NEVER GO TO LFS
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# These are read by `include_bytes!` / `include_str!` at COMPILE time. The Rust
# compiler reads whatever bytes are on disk; it has no idea what LFS is. On a
# clone made without git-lfs installed, an LFS-tracked file checks out as a
# ~130-byte pointer text file ("version https://git-lfs.github.com/spec/v1 ...").
# The build would then succeed and embed the pointer text as the splash PNG /
# the Inter font / an icon — a silently broken binary rather than a build error.
# That failure mode is far worse than a 1.6 MB blob in history.
#
# `-filter -diff -merge` pins them out of LFS even if a broad rule is added above.
#
# Sites (verified 2026-08-02):
#   ui/crates/nguo-splash/src/lib.rs:58,59,79   splash PNG, brand SVG, Inter TTF
#   ui/crates/nguo-gpu/src/overlay.rs:23         Space Mono TTF (the egui overlay's only font)
#   ui/crates/nguo-ui-widgets/src/icon.rs:103   include_bytes!(concat!("../../../assets/icons/", $file, ".svg"))
#   ui/crates/nguo-viewport3d/src/renderer.rs, ui/crates/nguo-gpu/src/blit.rs,
#   core-engine/crates/engine-gpu/src/*.rs      include_str! on *.wgsl (text, never LFS)
ui/assets/images/splash_screen_image.png -filter -diff -merge binary
ui/assets/fonts/Inter-Regular.ttf        -filter -diff -merge binary
ui/assets/fonts/SpaceMono-Regular.ttf    -filter -diff -merge binary
ui/assets/icons/**                       -filter -diff -merge text eol=lf
ui/assets/brand-icon/**                  -filter -diff -merge text eol=lf

